<!DOCTYPE html>
<!-- Quantum HTML + CSS example 01_text_elements/05: Code, kbd, samp and var -->
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Code, kbd, samp and var</title>
  <style>
    *, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }
    body {
      margin: 0;
      font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif;
      line-height: 1.5;
      color: #1f2933;
      background: #f5f7fa;
    }
    .demo { max-width: 60rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2rem 1.25rem; }
    .demo > h1 { margin: 0 0 0.25rem; font-size: 2rem; }
    .lead { margin: 0 0 2rem; color: #52606d; }

    .card { background: #fff; border-radius: 12px; padding: 1.5rem; box-shadow: 0 1px 3px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.12); }
    code, kbd, samp { font-family: ui-monospace, "Cascadia Code", Consolas, monospace; font-size: 0.95em; }
    code { background: #f1f5f9; padding: 0.1em 0.35em; border-radius: 4px; }
    kbd { border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; border-bottom-width: 3px; border-radius: 4px; padding: 0 0.35em; background: #fff; }
    samp { color: #047857; }
    var { font-family: Georgia, serif; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <main class="demo">
    <h1>Code, kbd, samp and var</h1>
    <p class="lead">Elements for talking about computers.</p>
    <section class="card">
      <p>Call <code>print()</code> to write a line.</p>
      <p>Save with <kbd>Ctrl</kbd> + <kbd>S</kbd>.</p>
      <p>The program answers <samp>Hello, world!</samp></p>
      <p>The area is <var>w</var> &times; <var>h</var>.</p>
    </section>
  </main>
</body>
</html>
